{% comment %}
  Package comparison table.

  A REAL <table>, with <th scope="col"> on the plans and <th scope="row"> on
  the feature names. That is what lets a screen reader announce a cell as
  "SUF-CPT + Seminar Bundle, CEUs earned, 1.1" rather than reading out a bare
  "1.1" with no idea which plan or which feature it belongs to. The mockup's
  markup is presentational -- all <td> and a header row of <th> with no scope --
  and that difference is the whole reason to build it as a table at all.

  THE SCROLL CONTAINER IS FOCUSABLE. It scrolls horizontally on narrow screens,
  and a scrollable region that cannot be reached by keyboard is unreachable
  content. tabindex="0" plus role="region" and a label make it a stop in the
  tab order that responds to arrow keys, with a visible focus ring saying so.

  VALUES. Each feature row holds one value per plan column:
      blank    -> "not included" (an em dash, plus hidden text)
      yes      -> the slash tick, plus hidden "Included"
      anything -> printed as written ("3 months", "1.1", "<b>Lifetime</b>")
  The two marks are aria-hidden; the meaning is in the hidden text beside them.

  NOT PORTED: the mockup's column-hover JavaScript, which tinted a whole column
  on mouseover. It is a hover-only affordance, so keyboard and touch users
  never get it, and the featured column is already marked permanently. A script
  that helps only mouse users scan is not worth the script.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign plans = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'plan'
  assign rows = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'row'
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | handle
  assign table_class = 'suf-ctable'
  if plans.size < 3
    assign table_class = table_class | append: ' suf-ctable--narrow'
  endif
-%}

<div class="suf-section" {% if anchor != blank %}id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <div class="suf-section__head">
        <h2>{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.heading %}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.aside != blank -%}
          <p class="suf-section__aside">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.aside %}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div
      class="suf-ctable-wrap"
      role="region"
      aria-label="{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Package comparison' | strip_html | escape }}"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <table class="{{ table_class }}">
        <caption class="suf-visually-hidden">
          {{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Package comparison' | strip_html }}
        </caption>

        <thead>
          <tr>
            <td class="suf-ctable__corner"></td>
            {%- for plan in plans -%}
              <th
                scope="col"
                class="suf-ctable__plan{% if plan.settings.featured %} suf-ctable__plan--featured{% endif %}"
                {{ plan.shopify_attributes }}
              >
                {%- if plan.settings.featured and plan.settings.flag != blank -%}
                  <span class="suf-ctable__flag">{{ plan.settings.flag | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="suf-ctable__name">{% render 'suf-nb', text: plan.settings.name %}</span>
                {%- if plan.settings.desc != blank -%}
                  <span class="suf-ctable__desc">{% render 'suf-nb', text: plan.settings.desc %}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if plan.settings.price != blank -%}
                  <span class="suf-ctable__price">{{ plan.settings.price | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if plan.settings.was != blank -%}
                  <span class="suf-ctable__was">{{ plan.settings.was | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </th>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
          {%- for row in rows -%}
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="suf-ctable__feature">
                {%- render 'suf-nb', text: row.settings.label -%}
              </th>
              {%- for plan in plans -%}
                {%- liquid
                  case forloop.index
                    when 1
                      assign value = row.settings.value_1
                    when 2
                      assign value = row.settings.value_2
                    else
                      assign value = row.settings.value_3
                  endcase
                  assign flag = value | downcase | strip
                -%}
                <td>
                  {%- if value == blank -%}
                    <span class="suf-ctable__no" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>
                    <span class="suf-visually-hidden">Not included</span>
                  {%- elsif flag == 'yes' -%}
                    <span class="suf-ctable__yes" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="suf-visually-hidden">Included</span>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- render 'suf-nb', text: value -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </td>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </tr>
          {%- endfor -%}

          <tr>
            <td></td>
            {%- for plan in plans -%}
              <td class="suf-ctable__cta">
                {%- comment -%}
                  SELLS IN PLACE WHEN A PRODUCT IS PICKED, exactly as suf-cert
                  and suf-guides do. A column that names a price and says "Buy
                  Now" should buy the thing, not route to a product page that
                  says it again.

                  The column stays a LINK when no product is set. That is not a
                  fallback for tidiness -- some columns genuinely are not one
                  purchasable item ("pick your two at checkout", or a package
                  whose price is quoted rather than transacted), and those need
                  somewhere to send people instead.

                  A <form> cannot live inside an <a>, which is why this is a
                  branch rather than a link wrapping a button -- the same
                  constraint written up for the product cards in
                  docs/redesign-open-items.md.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign plan_product = plan.settings.product -%}

                {%- if plan_product != blank -%}
                  {%- if plan_product.available -%}
                    {%- assign plan_style = plan.settings.button_style | default: 'primary' -%}
                    {%- form 'product', plan_product, class: 'suf-ctable__form' -%}
                      <input
                        type="hidden"
                        name="id"
                        value="{{ plan_product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
                      >
                      {%- if plan.settings.go_to_checkout -%}
                        <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value="/checkout">
                      {%- endif -%}

                      {%- comment -%}
                        A SEMINAR CREDIT, STATED FROM A TABLE CELL THAT CANNOT
                        ASK.

                        The CE page and the CPT page both offer a picker before
                        the button, so a buyer there either names a date or
                        takes the credit, and either way the order says which.
                        There is no room for a select in a comparison column,
                        so this path can only ever produce the credit -- and
                        with no property at all, the order arrived silent.

                        A silent order is the failure mode worth avoiding: a
                        seminar bundle with no seminar line cannot be told
                        apart from one where the picker broke. Staff have to
                        work out from the product title alone that someone is
                        owed a seat.

                        The value MATCHES suf-seminar-options.liquid exactly.
                        Two spellings of one state would sort and filter as two
                        things in the admin, and this is the string staff scan
                        to find who still needs booking. Change one, change
                        both.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- if plan.settings.seminar_credit -%}
                        {%- comment -%}
                          The DEFAULT is the shared one-credit string. A column
                          overrides it only where the count is wrong -- the
                          Qualified Trainer Package carries three seminars, and
                          a line reading "Credit" singular would understate an
                          order by two seats.

                          A setting rather than a second hardcoded branch: the
                          next package with a different count is a checkbox and
                          a field, not another `elsif` here.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        <input
                          type="hidden"
                          name="properties[Seminar]"
                          value="{{ plan.settings.seminar_credit_value | default: 'Credit — to be booked later' | escape }}"
                        >
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <button
                        type="submit"
                        class="suf-btn suf-btn--{{ plan_style }}"
                        name="add"
                      >
                        {{- plan.settings.button_label | default: 'Buy Now' | escape -}}
                      </button>
                    {%- endform -%}
                  {%- else -%}
                    <p class="suf-btn-micro">Currently unavailable.</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- elsif plan.settings.button_label != blank and plan.settings.button_url != blank -%}
                  <a
                    class="suf-btn suf-btn--{{ plan.settings.button_style | default: 'primary' }}"
                    href="{{ plan.settings.button_url }}"
                  >
                    {{- plan.settings.button_label | escape -}}
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if plan.settings.micro != blank -%}
                  <p class="suf-btn-micro">{{ plan.settings.micro | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </td>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
      <div class="suf-tnote">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.note %}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Comparison table (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 16,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "Section heading" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "aside", "label": "Supporting note" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor",
      "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Lets a button elsewhere link here, e.g. \"new-trainers\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "Note under the table",
      "info": "Centred fine print, e.g. what the price does not cover."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "plan",
      "name": "Plan (column)",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "name", "label": "Name" },
        { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "desc", "label": "One-line description" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "price", "label": "Price" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "was",
          "label": "Price comparison",
          "info": "e.g. \"$X,XXX bought separately\"."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "featured",
          "label": "Featured column",
          "info": "Navy, outlined top to bottom. Use on ONE column -- two recommendations is none.",
          "default": false
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "flag", "label": "Flag text", "default": "Most Popular" },
        {
          "type": "product",
          "id": "product",
          "label": "Product",
          "info": "Set this and the column SELLS IN PLACE -- the button becomes a real add-to-cart form, as on the certification rows and study guide cards. Leave empty for a column that is not one purchasable item, and it falls back to the link below. The price shown is still the typed one above, not the product's."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "go_to_checkout",
          "label": "Skip the cart",
          "info": "Adds return_to=/checkout, so the button goes straight to checkout instead of the cart. Only applies when a product is set.",
          "default": true
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "seminar_credit",
          "label": "Includes a seminar credit",
          "info": "Tags the order \"Seminar: Credit -- to be booked later\", because a table column has no room to ask which one. Tick it only where the package actually includes a seminar. Only applies when a product is set.",
          "default": false
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "seminar_credit_value",
          "label": "Credit wording",
          "info": "Leave empty unless the package carries MORE THAN ONE seminar -- \"Credit -- to be booked later\" would then understate the order. Keep the wording close to the default: this is the text staff scan to find who still needs booking, and two spellings of one state sort as two things."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Buy Now" },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "button_url",
          "label": "Button link",
          "info": "Used ONLY when no product is set above."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "button_style",
          "label": "Button style",
          "options": [
            { "value": "primary", "label": "Filled red" },
            { "value": "ghost", "label": "Outline" }
          ],
          "default": "primary"
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "micro", "label": "Fine print under the button" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "name": "Feature (row)",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "label", "label": "Feature" },
        {
          "type": "inline_richtext",
          "id": "value_1",
          "label": "Column 1",
          "info": "Leave blank for \"not included\". Type yes for a tick. Anything else prints as written."
        },
        { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "value_2", "label": "Column 2" },
        { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "value_3", "label": "Column 3" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Comparison table (SUF)",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "plan" },
        { "type": "plan" },
        { "type": "row" },
        { "type": "row" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
